<title>UK: UK Mar-May primary fuel output drops 2.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>UK Mar-May primary fuel output drops 2.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's primary fuel production in the three months from March to May fell by 2.6 percent from the same period in 1996, provisional Department of Trade and Industry figures showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Of total production of 70 million tonnes of oil equivalent, primary electricity output rose by 8.4 percent, while production of coal, oil and natural gas fell by 4.1 percent, 0.8 percent, and 7.6 percent respectively.</p>
<p>&quot;The increase in primary electricity production reflected increased output from nuclear stations of 7.5 percent. Gas production was lower as a result of lower demand for gas as a heating fuel during the warmer weather at the beginning of 1997,&quot; the DTI said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5387</p>
</text>
